# rclone exclude file for the Google Drive mirror described in SETUP.md.
#
# Point of this file: keep the Drive mirror's exclusions roughly matched to
# your .gitignore, EXCEPT for files that are too large for GitHub (>100MB) —
# leave those OUT of this list so Drive (which has no size cap) still gets
# them. Copy this to .claude/rclone-exclude.txt and edit for your own repo.

.git/**
.claude/**

# Editor/IDE caches, build artifacts, anything else your .gitignore excludes
# for being regenerable rather than source content:
# **/.Rproj.user/**
# node_modules/**

# Anything sensitive that should never leave this machine or its backups —
# match these to your .gitignore's own sensitive-file exclusions:
# grant stuff/*.pdf
# secrets/**

# A large file this machine doesn't have a local copy of should NOT be
# excluded here just because it's missing locally — that's backwards, and
# it's exactly the mistake that argues for `rclone copy` over `rclone sync`
# in the first place (see SETUP.md's "backup & sync infrastructure" section,
# and the slide deck's "lesson learned" slide, for the incident that
# prompted that rule). Only list a big Drive-only file here if THIS
# machine genuinely never has, and never will have, its own local copy:
# Zotero/some-huge-file-too-big-for-github.pdf
